ehicle_unit_gamma will not be available. Goal wants vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma true. So we cannot allocate gamma to shift_candidate_beta if we need it available. Actually goal wants vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma true. So we must not allocate gamma to any candidate after making it available. But shift_candidate_beta needs vehicle_allocated and candidate_vehicle_linked to vehicle_unit_gamma per goal. So we have a contradiction again: shift_candidate_beta needs vehicle allocated to gamma, but goal also wants vehicle_available gamma true. However after dispatching shift_candidate_beta, vehicle_available gamma becomes true again (since dispatch effect adds vehicle_available). So we could allocate gamma to shift_candidate_beta, then dispatch shift_candidate_beta, making vehicle_available gamma true again. Meanwhile vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta stays true, candidate_vehicle_linked stays true. So after dispatch, vehicle_available gamma true (as desired). Good! So we need to dispatch shift_candidate_beta after allocating its vehicle.

